dbclient
Usage: dbclient [-i KEYFILE] [-p PORT] [-l USER] [USER@]HOST [COMMAND]

Log in to another machine over SSH, or run one command there.

	-i FILE		identity (private key) to authenticate with
	-p PORT		remote port
	-l USER		remote username
	-J CMD		proxy through a command
	-N		do not run a command (just forward ports)
	-L LPORT:HOST:PORT	forward a local port to a remote host:port
	-R RPORT:HOST:PORT	forward a remote port back to a local host:port
	-f		background after authenticating

	dbclient -i /state/id root@10.9.0.1
	dbclient -i /state/id root@10.9.0.1 'abduco -a work'

The last form is how you drop straight back into a running session: ssh
in and attach to abduco in one command.

See also: dropbear, dropbearkey, wg, abduco
